    "description": "# napari-reco-plugin\r\n\r\nA [napari](https://napari.org) plugin for parallel-beam tomographic reconstruction with the\r\n[ASTRA Toolbox](https://www.astra-toolbox.com/), with single-distance **Paganin** phase retrieval.\r\n\r\n- Reconstruction algorithms: **FBP, BP, SIRT, SART, CGLS**, on GPU (CUDA) or CPU.\r\n- Standard (180\u00b0 or 360\u00b0) and **half acquisition** (offset rotation axis, 360\u00b0) scans.\r\n- Flat/dark-field and double flat-field correction, measured angles read from `.nxs` files.\r\n- Centre-of-rotation tools: COR scan on one slice, automatic global COR (half acquisition).\r\n- **Big Data** mode: batch processing with lazy loading, result written to a temporary HDF5 file.\r\n- Readers for `.nxs` / `.tdf` (HDF5); writers for `.tif` and `.raw` (+ processing history as JSON).\r\n\r\nEverything also runs **without a GPU**: CuPy is optional (NumPy/SciPy are used instead) and\r\nASTRA's CPU algorithms are used when CUDA is not available.\r\n\r\n## Installation\r\n\r\n### pip\r\n\r\n```bash\r\npip install \"napari-reco-plugin[astra]\"        # plugin + ASTRA Toolbox\r\npip install cupy-cuda12x                       # optional: GPU arrays (or cupy-cuda11x)\r\n```\r\n\r\n### conda (recommended, GPU or CPU)\r\n\r\nFrom a clone of this repository, create a dedicated environment with everything\r\n(napari, ASTRA, CuPy, all from conda-forge) and the plugin in editable mode:\r\n\r\n```bash\r\nconda env create -f environment.yml\r\nconda activate napari-reco\r\nnapari\r\n```\r\n\r\nASTRA and CuPy use CUDA when an NVIDIA driver is present, otherwise the CPU.\r\nAvoid mixing Qt bindings in one environment (e.g. PyQt5 and PySide6): napari \u2265 0.10 needs Qt 6.\r\n\r\n### From source (development)\r\n\r\n```bash\r\ngit clone https://github.com/Clementcmoi/Reconstruction-napari-plugin.git\r\ncd Reconstruction-napari-plugin\r\npip install -e \".[testing]\"\r\n```\r\n\r\nThe array backend in use (`cupy (GPU)` or `numpy (CPU)`) is shown at the bottom of the\r\n*Reconstruction Algorithm* section. Set `RECO_PLUGIN_BACKEND=numpy` to force the CPU.\r\n\r\n## Usage\r\n\r\nStart napari, open a `.nxs`/`.tdf` file (projections, flats and darks become layers), then\r\n**Plugins \u203a Reconstruction Plugin \u203a Reconstruction**.\r\n\r\nTypical workflow in the *Reconstruction* panel:\r\n\r\n1. **Sample Selection** \u2013 choose the projection layer (angles \u00d7 rows \u00d7 columns). *Slice* is a\r\n   detector row (0 \u2026 rows \u2212 1).\r\n2. **Preprocessing** \u2013 tick *Flatfield* / *Darkfield* and choose their layers. *Apply* creates a\r\n   `preprocess_\u2026` layer, but it is optional: every action applies the correction itself.\r\n3. **Paganin** \u2013 energy (keV), distance (m), \u03b4/\u03b2, optional unsharp mask and outlier cleaning.\r\n   *Apply* creates a `paganin_\u2026_db<\u03b4/\u03b2>` layer (optional as well).\r\n4. **Center of Rotation** \u2013 *Standard*: enter a COR range and *Try Center of Rotation* (one\r\n   frame per COR value, listed in the layer metadata). *Half acquisition*: *Find Global Center of\r\n   Rotation*, then refine with *Try Center of Rotation* (\u00b1 delta around the value).\r\n5. **Reconstruction Algorithm** \u2013 algorithm, GPU or CPU, pixel size (m, also used for the units).\r\n6. **Process** \u2013 *Process one slice* or *Process all slices* (*Big Data* for volumes that do not\r\n   fit in RAM).\r\n\r\nResults carry their full processing history in the layer metadata, saved next to the image by\r\nthe `.tif` and `.raw` writers.\r\n\r\n### Good to know\r\n\r\n- **Parameters are read when you click.** Changing \u03b4/\u03b2 (or any field) is always taken into\r\n  account. A layer already filtered with Paganin is reused only if its parameters match the\r\n  current ones; otherwise the plugin goes back to the layer it was computed from, so Paganin is\r\n  never applied twice.\r\n- **Units:** pixel size and distance are in **metres** (0.65 \u00b5m \u2192 `0.65e-6`, 50 mm \u2192 `0.05`);\r\n  values that look like \u00b5m or mm are rejected, because they make \u03b4/\u03b2 seem to have no effect.\r\n  Commas are accepted as decimal separators. With a pixel size, reconstructions are in mm\u207b\u00b9.\r\n- **Without Paganin**, flat-field corrected transmissions I/I\u2080 are converted to attenuation\r\n  \u2212ln(I/I\u2080) before reconstruction (Paganin's output already is an attenuation).\r\n- The pixel size appears in the *Paganin* and *Reconstruction Algorithm* sections: it is the\r\n  same field (editing one updates the other).\r\n- **COR convention:** standard acquisition = position of the axis on the detector (pixels);\r\n  half acquisition = distance from the left detector edge to the axis (the overlap is 2 \u00d7 COR).\r\n- **SART iterations** are full sweeps over all projections.\r\n- **Big Data:** the temporary HDF5 output is deleted when its layer is removed or napari closes.\r\n  Datasets larger than `RECO_PLUGIN_LAZY_GB` (default 4 GB) are opened lazily by the reader.\r\n\r\n## Troubleshooting\r\n\r\n| Symptom | Cause / fix |\r\n| --- | --- |\r\n| Changing \u03b4/\u03b2 changes nothing | Check the units: the pixel size must be in metres (e.g. `0.65e-6`). |\r\n| *Use GPU (CUDA)* is greyed out | ASTRA cannot use CUDA on this machine: CPU algorithms are used. |\r\n| \"Another processing is still running\" | One job at a time; wait for the *Processing* window to close. |\r\n| \"no 1D dataset of N angles\" | Untick *Use the measured angles*, or check the file contains them. |\r\n\r\n## Development\r\n\r\n```bash\r\npip install -e \".[testing]\"\r\npytest            # CPU backend, offscreen Qt: no GPU or display needed\r\n```\r\n\r\nProject layout:\r\n\r\n```\r\nsrc/reco_plugin/\r\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 _widget.py, ui_sections.py           # Qt panel\r\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 _link.py                             # parameters \u2192 processing (background threads)\r\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 _reader.py, _writer.py, napari.yaml  # napari reader / writers / manifest\r\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 processing/                          # numerical code (Paganin, sinograms, COR, ASTRA)\r\n\u2514\u2500\u2500 utils/                               # backend (CuPy/NumPy), parameters, layers, Qt helpers\r\ntests/                                   # pytest suite\r\nlaunchers/                               # Windows .bat templates to start napari\r\n```\r\n\r\nSee [CHANGELOG.md](CHANGELOG.md) for the list of changes.\r\n\r\n## License\r\n\r\nMIT \u2014 see [LICENSE](LICENSE). The ASTRA Toolbox itself is distributed under the GPLv3.\r\n",
